From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 16:39:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 144/148] fix(refinery): merge-push and batch land drop temp on
 every exit (gcp-fooz4)

Upstream #374 (220744b2) made the rebase step's `git checkout -b temp
origin/$BRANCH` exit-checked. A `temp` that outlives the merge-push step now
makes every later patrol STOP at the rebase step and drain, and the wisp is
poured --root-only, so the restarted refinery re-selects the same bead and
STOPs again until a human deletes `temp`. Our lanes left it on most stops:
merge-push.sh cleaned up only on 0 and 4 (statuses 2, 3, 5-9 and 11 left it,
including a landing whose bead write failed), and merge-batch.sh land cleaned
up only on 0.

merge-push.sh gains drop_temp_on_exit, run after main on every exit once the
bead's target is resolved. It uses the existing cleanup_temp: upstream's idiom
(checkout --detach onto origin/$TARGET, then branch -d || -D) with 0121's
detached-checkout rule. land sets the same marker once its manifest checks
pass, and cmd_land calls the same function. A usage or config error (status
1) returns before the target is known and still touches nothing.

The status-3 message and the formula's status-7 paragraph promised that a
later patrol would pick the branch back up, which the stranded temp
prevented. They now say what happens: temp is gone, nothing resumes at the
push, and the next patrol rebuilds temp in the rebase step and re-runs the
tests. The batch paragraph no longer says land cleans up only on 0.

Tests, each red against restack2's scripts and green after:
- test_refinery_merge_push.sh runs the whole script through the direct lane
  to statuses 2 (push did not advance; landed but bead write failed), 3, 6, 7
  and 8 and requires refs/heads/temp gone, plus a landing (0) and the status-1
  boundary (temp kept).
- test_refinery_merge_batch.sh asserts temp is gone after land statuses 2
  (left open, every member refused, the three status-2 guards), 6 and 7, and
  adds land cases for 3 (re-rebase conflict) and 5 (no-op). Status-1 guards
  keep temp. 22 cases.
- test_refinery_merge_lanes.sh checks after every real script run that no
  status but 1 left temp; against the old script that caught 7, 8, 9 (x6)
  and 11.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
